 "team_rankings": [],
 "notes": "Second read 2026-10-27: Southern Maine Middle School Relays (printed 'Souther Maine Middle School Relays', September 20, 2006, hosted by Traip Academy at Fort Foster); school names written '<town> Middle School' ('Messabesec' is Massabesic). Races 1-5 (one runner per school per heat) match the parse row for row; Open Race: the parse kept only the 13 rows whose time carries a minute (places 1, 10, 17, 31, 38, 43, 46, 50-55); the sheet prints the other times as bare seconds, the minute lost (places 2-9 '38'..'54' after 10:32; 11-16 '42'..'57' after 11:25; 18-30 and so on). The minute is recovered from the place order (every time is at or after the one before, and each bare number is read as seconds after the last printed minute, rolling to the next minute when the seconds fall): e.g. 2 Brown 10:38, 11 Finitz 11:42, 18 Nuttall 12:06 ('6'), 32 Brown 13:06, 47 Greenblatt 16:04 ('4'); every inferred time lies between its neighbours' printed full times (10:32 < ... < 11:25 < ... < 12:03 < ... < 13:01 < ... < 14:00 < ... < 15:11 < ... < 16:00 < ... < 17:56), so the minute is unambiguous. All 55 marked rows of the open race are written (places 1-55); places 56-63 (Laoureaux, Meier, Duncan, Willard, Rousselle, McGarey, Offermann, Fountain) have no mark and are left out. Place 35 'B. Nichols' is printed with school 'Marsh/Mess?': Buck Nichols is Marshwood Middle School in yorkcountymsjrboy (Nichols, Marshwood), smaamiddlerelaysboys 2007 and sacomiddleboys 2007-08, so Marshwood."
}